        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: సాధ్యం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాధ్యం — sādhyaṁ — \"possible; feasible\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఒక్క రోజులో ఆ పని సాధ్యం కాదు. okka rōjulō ā pani sādhyaṁ kādu. That job is not possible in a single day."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాధ్యం (sādhyaṁ) కాదు, it is not possible; సాధ్యమైనంత, as much as possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "సాధ్యం (sādhyaṁ) is borrowed from Sanskrit sādhya, \"to be mastered, won or managed\" (Monier-Williams), from sādh, \"to accomplish\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
